{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/749149-utterly-uninformed-questions-beast-the-primordial-x-lost-s-beast-kith","id":749149,"title":"Utterly uninformed questions - Beast the Primordial x Lost's Beast Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-02T07:48:18-08:00","id":749149,"title":"Utterly uninformed questions - Beast the Primordial x Lost's Beast Kith","content":"How similar or different can they be from each other?<br /> <br /> Could some of the begotten be confused with, if not outright be high wyrd &amp; low clarity lost of the Beast kith?<br /> <br /> Might there be a relation?<br /> <br /> Could the begotten be, if not deeply changed lost, some kind of true Fae, native of Hedge or a similar place?<br /> <br /> Pardon the ignorance in my questions, but the few teasers i have got about the Beast series, stuff of nightmares and etc, gives me more questions than answers, so i decided to outright post and ask about it.<br /> <br /> PS: On a little aside, how possible or even probable would it be for some regional brand of the &quot;Nosferatu&quot; type of vampires to have been spawned, direct or indirectly, by the actions of some sort of begotten or related entity instead of the usual shadow &amp; smoke owl suspect, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T08:22:51-08:00","id":749218,"title":"","content":"Maybe initially if the changeling is fairly new and uninformed.. however the similarities go only skin deep. Beasts don't have masks, their form is only seen when they manifest powers or when they are in their lairs. The creation of a beast is entirely different from a Changeling as well. Changelings are stolen and have the change forced upon them, while beasts were always different from the beginning.. they are simply devoured by the horror and reborn. They are conduits of the Primordial dream and have a supernatural connection to all monsters (minus GM demons) though the dark mother.<br /> <br /> It is easy for a beast to be confused with a True Fae, however. They shape the hedge just by being in it, and they are not truly constrained by conventional morality. Not to mention they're beings of nightmare, teaching humanity wisdom through fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T08:53:53-08:00","id":749239,"title":"","content":"Well, it's always <i>possible</i> to mistake a beast for almost anything, because they have a power that lets them camouflage themselves as anything they have kinship to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T09:50:52-08:00","id":749397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/749149-utterly-uninformed-questions-beast-the-primordial-x-lost-s-beast-kith?p=749218#post749218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe initially if the changeling is fairly new and uninformed.. however the similarities go only skin deep. Beasts don't have masks, their form is only seen when they manifest powers or when they are in their lairs. The creation of a beast is entirely different from a Changeling as well. Changelings are stolen and have the change forced upon them, while beasts were always different from the beginning.. they are simply devoured by the horror and reborn. They are conduits of the Primordial dream and have a supernatural connection to all monsters (minus GM demons) though the dark mother.<br /> <br /> It is easy for a beast to be confused with a True Fae, however. They shape the hedge just by being in it, and they are not truly constrained by conventional morality. Not to mention they're beings of nightmare, teaching humanity wisdom through fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a connection to the True Fae and other natives of the Hedge might be possible, you think?<br /> Also, what is the Dark Mother? Would she have anything to do with the Crone's idea of Mother of Monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:02:42-08:00","id":749413,"title":"","content":"The dark mother is indeed similar to the crone's idea of the mother of monsters. The dark mother IS the mother of all monsters according to beasts. This includes true fae (and changelings), vampires, werewolves, mages, and yes.. even prometheans. (and slashers and fetches..... the list goes on..) Which means.. the ultimate answer of are they related/connected is &quot;yes&quot; but also &quot;Probably not in the way you think they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind the Primordial Dream has little or nothing to do with the Hedge or Arcadia, but it does at least connect to the hedge. It could be thought that the True Fae might have their origins in ancient beasts who went a little off the beaten path.. or they could be mages that had moved on to the supernal realm of Arcadia, and had become twisted over time. It is deliberately ambigous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":2451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","user":"Windrave","date":". 11-02-2015, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:06:49-08:00","id":749419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/749149-utterly-uninformed-questions-beast-the-primordial-x-lost-s-beast-kith?p=749397#post749397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a connection to the True Fae and other natives of the Hedge might be possible, you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Possible&quot; is a bit of an understatement relative to &quot;already exists.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what is the Dark Mother? Would she have anything to do with the Crone's idea of Mother of Monsters? </div> </div> </div>The Dark Mother is, according to the lore of the Begotten, the <i>first</i> great monster. She's spawned countless nightmares since the earliest days of humanity and Beasts posit that virtually every other kind of supernatural being draws descent from her in some fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:34:13-08:00","id":749452,"title":"","content":"Although bear in mind that the Dark Mother is an <i>astral</i> entity, and so when they say that all other monsters are descended from her that could well be in a conceptual, archetype sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:38:10-08:00","id":749457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/749149-utterly-uninformed-questions-beast-the-primordial-x-lost-s-beast-kith?p=749397#post749397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a connection to the True Fae and other natives of the Hedge might be possible, you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its exact nature is not explicitly spelled out beyond the basics of Beasts considering all the supernaturals in the World of Darkness family, but there is a suspiciously strong connection to the True Fae, yes, up to and including the fact that Beasts warp the Hedge in exactly the same way. Beasts are literally living nightmares encased in human flesh, and while they have no Contracts in the Changeling sense (except perhaps those of kinship, from a certain point of view), a high-Lair Beast is one of the few things that can deal with the Gentry on something approaching even terms. The following should be taken with a grain of salt, but you may find it a useful metaphor: if the Gentle Folk are the Seelie, you can think of the Nightmare that literally is a Beast's soul as being Unseelie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T11:08:32-08:00","id":749496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/749149-utterly-uninformed-questions-beast-the-primordial-x-lost-s-beast-kith?p=749457#post749457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its exact nature is not explicitly spelled out beyond the basics of Beasts considering all the supernaturals in the World of Darkness family, but there is a suspiciously strong connection to the True Fae, yes, up to and including the fact that Beasts warp the Hedge in exactly the same way. Beasts are literally living nightmares encased in human flesh, and while they have no Contracts in the Changeling sense (except perhaps those of kinship, from a certain point of view), a high-Lair Beast is one of the few things that can deal with the Gentry on something approaching even terms. The following should be taken with a grain of salt, but you may find it a useful metaphor: if the Gentle Folk are the Seelie, you can think of the Nightmare that literally is a Beast's soul as being Unseelie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had seen a similar comparison somewhere else and it is indeed helpful. Offers a variety of ideas too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}